---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';


const path = '/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-activecampaign';
const title = 'Yotpo Email & SMS to ActiveCampaign for Shopify: 2026 Migration';
const desc = 'Evaluate ActiveCampaign after Yotpo messaging retirement: Shopify history, wholesale CRM handoffs, permission records and queued campaigns.';

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can a Shopify store still choose Yotpo Email & SMS in 2026?",
    "answer": "Yotpo announced full Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025, and its messaging endpoint now reports decommissioning. This is a migration decision. Reviews and Loyalty are separate products; keeping them does not restore the retired messaging service."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I move messaging to ActiveCampaign and keep Yotpo Reviews?",
    "answer": "Plan Reviews as a separate service with its own request sender and schedule. Prove any required review events or fields reach ActiveCampaign before using them in branches. A Shopify connection alone does not establish that review data or loyalty balances transfer."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should I price ActiveCampaign for 18,000 contacts?",
    "answer": "Request a quote for your eligible contact population, planned sends, sales users and required CRM features. Add migration work, any separate SMS service, and retained Reviews or Loyalty subscriptions. Old Yotpo invoices are a historical baseline, not an available renewal offer."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does Shopify order history replace Yotpo messaging history?",
    "answer": "No. Shopify order records can support purchase-based decisions, but they do not reconstruct Yotpo campaign engagement, consent evidence or automation position. Keep a source and destination map for each required asset and mark unavailable history explicitly."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should I also consider Sequenzy?",
    "answer": "Include Sequenzy in a separate evaluation if your requirement is primarily lifecycle email. Demonstrate your Shopify events, eligibility rules, exits and operating cost in the offered setup. Do not assume it replaces wholesale CRM, Yotpo history or review integrations."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should wholesale merchants prove in ActiveCampaign?",
    "answer": "Prove who owns a lead, how a quote task is created, and how a purchase or reply ends promotional follow-up. Test a buyer who also shops as a consumer. A company field or wholesale tag alone does not prove account-level routing, permissions or deal ownership."
  },
  {
    "question": "Who should send review and loyalty messages after migration?",
    "answer": "Assign each request or reward notice to an explicit owner. Preserve Reviews and Loyalty configuration separately from messaging migration. Prove event availability and duplicate prevention before enabling a replacement sender; do not assume a points balance is a marketing permission."
  },
  {
    "question": "What test should decide whether ActiveCampaign fits?",
    "answer": "Use a proposed wholesale sample-to-order exercise: import historical purchases with marketing disabled, assign a sales owner, then place a new order while a reminder waits. Verify no historical replay, no duplicate deal or reminder, correct channel permission and a visible record of cancellation. No test results are claimed here."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a><span class="mx-2 text-[#5d3a1d]">/</span><span>Yotpo Email & SMS vs ActiveCampaign</span></nav>
      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="catalog-kicker">Migration decision</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Yotpo Email & SMS to ActiveCampaign for Shopify</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">For a Shopify merchant with wholesale sales alongside consumer orders, the useful question is whether ActiveCampaign can join purchase activity to a maintainable sales handoff. Yotpo messaging is retired. Moving contacts is only one part of rebuilding that workflow; review requests, loyalty notices and unfinished sales conversations need separate decisions.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="mt-12 max-w-4xl">
        <TldrBox picks={[
          { label: 'Existing Yotpo messaging', tool: 'Migration required', reason: 'The service is decommissioned; establish what records you still hold.' },
          { label: 'Wholesale sales handoff', tool: 'Evaluate ActiveCampaign', reason: 'Demonstrate purchase-to-sales routing in the quoted configuration.' },
          { label: 'Reviews and Loyalty', tool: 'Separate ownership', reason: 'Retain or replace these products independently of messaging.' },
        ]} />
      </div>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>The retirement changes the decision</h2>
        <p>Yotpo's <a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">September 2025 announcement</a> scheduled Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025 and named Attentive and Omnisend as migration partners. The <a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">current service notice</a> says the SMS application and background services are decommissioned. ActiveCampaign is a destination to assess independently, rather than one of those named partners. Do not assume the partner migration tools or historical offers apply to it.</p>
        <p>If migration was deferred, inventory existing exports, local templates and the current sender first. Do not write a plan that depends on logging into the retired dashboard. Record missing assets and ask the supplier what recovery remains possible; no recovery access is established here. Keep Yotpo Reviews and Loyalty contracts and settings in a separate inventory.</p>
        <h2>What the Shopify connection supplies</h2>
        <p>ActiveCampaign's <a class="link" href="https://help.activecampaign.com/hc/en-us/articles/360012461899-Data-synced-from-the-ActiveCampaign-Shopify-integration">Shopify data documentation</a> describes order, product, customer and abandoned-cart sync, including store tags and company-to-account mapping. It excludes draft orders. It also syncs contacts who did not opt into marketing, so record presence cannot be your send criterion. Historical sync is plan restricted; obtain confirmation for the plan quoted today.</p>
        <p>For wholesale, a missing draft quote matters: a buyer waiting for a negotiated order may look inactive if your automation sees only completed purchases. Choose a source for quote status and an owner for updating it. Treat the following requirements as an acceptance specification, not a claim that the default integration supplies them.</p>
        <h2>Map the sales handoff before building email</h2>
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Business fact</th><th>Destination requirement</th><th>Failure to expose</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Wholesale application</td><td>Named owner, application state and source record</td><td>A generic customer tag routes an unapproved buyer into trade offers</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Sample requested</td><td>One open follow-up linked to the right buyer and account</td><td>Reimport creates another task for the same sample</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Quote pending</td><td>Sales-controlled pause with a visible reason</td><td>Consumer recovery discounts undermine a negotiated quote</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Purchase completed</td><td>Close or update the appropriate follow-up and cancel its reminder</td><td>A retail accessory purchase incorrectly closes the wholesale opportunity</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Marketing withdrawn</td><td>Channel-specific suppression checked before promotional dispatch</td><td>A sales tag restores a previously withdrawn subscription</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>Ask for the exact CRM, automation and user entitlements in the offer. Have the person covering the sales inbox demonstrate reassignment and explain what happens when an owner leaves. If the business only needs newsletters and purchase follow-ups, maintaining this sales model may add work without improving the customer journey.</p>
        <h2>Keep permission, order history and message history distinct</h2>
        <p>Build a migration ledger with source identifier, export date, channel, subscription state, evidence location, destination field and import result. Keep suppression and withdrawal records alongside eligible subscribers. A phone number, loyalty membership or order does not establish permission for a new promotional channel. Resolve conflicting records before activation rather than treating the newest import as permission.</p>
        <p>Shopify orders can rebuild purchase segments; they cannot recreate which Yotpo email was opened or which step a customer was waiting in. Mark missing engagement as unknown, not disengaged. Avoid restarting a welcome offer because a migrated customer lacks a destination campaign history. Preserve original order identifiers and dates, and inspect whether historical imports can enter automations before importing at scale.</p>
        <h2>Reconcile unfinished work, including work outside Yotpo</h2>
        <p>The retired sender cannot be relied on to complete old waits. List pending sample follow-ups, abandoned carts and scheduled promotions from whatever records remain. For each, choose cancel, rebuild with current eligibility, or hand to a named operator. Check the present ESP, Shopify automations and sales CRM for replacement jobs already running. Recreating an old sequence without this reconciliation can duplicate a message that another system has taken over.</p>
        <p>Keep review collection under its designated owner while migrating promotional follow-up. Document whether a review request belongs to Yotpo Reviews or a destination workflow. For Loyalty, separately map reward notification, balance source, expiry and redemption links. Do not put stale exported balances in a campaign or assume the Shopify connector carries those events. Require a demonstrated route for every review or loyalty condition used in an automation.</p>
        <h2>Proposed test: a wholesale sample becomes an order</h2>
        <p>Use test identities and disabled promotional delivery while preparing this exercise. Create a buyer with a historical sample order and a current wholesale enquiry. Import the historical order first: expected result is a usable purchase record with no new sample reminder. Submit the enquiry twice: expected result is one assigned follow-up, with duplicate handling visible to the operator.</p>
        <p>Queue the sample reminder, then create a qualifying wholesale order. The expected result is cancellation of that reminder and an updated sales task. Repeat with an unrelated retail purchase: the wholesale opportunity should remain open unless your documented policy says otherwise. This distinction tests the actual handoff instead of merely checking that a purchase event exists.</p>
        <p>Finally withdraw email permission while the reminder waits, reassign the owner and replay the original event. Inspect the pending queue and contact record: withdrawal must still prevent promotional email, reassignment must preserve context, and replay must not create another task. Test SMS separately if required. Keep order service notices on their intended service route. Record failures and repair them before activating the affected automation; these are proposed checks, not performed measurements.</p>
        <h2>Compare the complete operating cost</h2>
        <p>Quote contacts and sends using the population that will actually be eligible, including seasonal changes. Ask how suppressed records, users, sales features, SMS and overages are billed. Add any retained Reviews and Loyalty subscriptions and the work to rebuild templates, fields and integrations. Do not compare an old bundled Yotpo invoice against a headline entry price.</p>
        <p>As a hypothetical planning calculation, eight hours of migration work at $60 per hour is $480 once; two hours of monthly maintenance at the same rate is $120 per month, or $1,440 per year. These are illustrative labor inputs, not supplier prices or measured effort. Replace them with an inventory-based estimate and include the annual subscription quote separately. See <a class="link" href="/guides/pricing-models">pricing models</a> for the billing framework.</p>
        <h2>When ActiveCampaign earns the extra work</h2>
        <p>Shortlist ActiveCampaign when named sales ownership and purchase-driven follow-up are concrete requirements, and the proposed configuration passes the sample-to-order exercise. If CRM is incidental, evaluate a simpler lifecycle setup against the same essential purchase and permission rules. Sequenzy can be another candidate for that evaluation; require demonstrated Shopify event coverage and operating cost rather than assuming a migration or CRM replacement.</p>
        <p>The acceptance record should show where each legacy asset went, which jobs were cancelled, which Reviews and Loyalty services remain, and who owns failures. Choose on that evidence and the quoted configuration. No winner, delivery improvement or revenue lift has been established by this article. Use the <a class="link" href="/guides/selection-framework">selection framework</a> to turn unresolved requirements into a destination decision.</p>
      </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/drip-vs-activecampaign">Drip vs ActiveCampaign</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/privy-vs-activecampaign">Privy vs ActiveCampaign</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-drip">Yotpo vs Drip</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/b2b-wholesale">Email tools for B2B wholesale</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Yotpo Email & SMS vs ActiveCampaign FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
